{"records":[{"id":"4r55hvz87r","title":"Negative DNA supercoiling induces genome-wide Cas9 off-target activity. Newton MD et al","description":"CRISPR/Cas9 is a powerful gene-editing technology, however off-target activity remains an important consideration for therapeutic applications. We have previous-ly shown that force stretching DNA induces off-target activity and hypothesised that distortions of the DNA topology in vivo, such as negative DNA supercoiling, could reduce Cas9 specificity. Using single-molecule optical-tweezers, we demonstrate that negative supercoiling λ-DNA induces sequence-specific Cas9 off-target bind-ing at multiple sites, even at low forces. Using an adapted CIRCLE-seq approach, we detect over 10,000 negative supercoiling induced Cas9 off-target double-strand breaks genome wide, caused by increased mismatch tolerance. We further demon-strate in vivo that directed local DNA distortion increases off-target activity in cells and that induced off-target events can be detected during Cas9 genome-editing. These data demonstrate that Cas9 off-target activity is regulated by DNA topology in vitro and in vivo, suggesting that cellular processes, such as transcription and replication, could induce off-target activity at previously overlooked sites. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-03-12T08:20:22.495Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4r55hvz87r","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4r55hvz87r"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Matt","last_name":"Newton","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biochemistry","Molecular Biology","Single Molecule Imaging","Next Generation Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9","Genome Editing"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"r79ngfdb56","title":"High-throughput sequencing of Precise CRISPR/Cas9-targeted Recessive Dystrophic Epidermolysis Bullosa immortalised keratinocytes (Ion Torrent)","description":"In this study, the COL7A1 on-target (exon 73) was analysed for precise CRISPR/Cas9 activity. \nNGS data was assessed in CRISPR/Cas9-treated immortalised patient keratinocytes\nDespite high on-target activity, high homgeneity of DSB repair outcomes was observed at the nuclease target site. This should result in efficient reframing of the gene, with minimal divergence from the wild-type sequence.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-09-20T10:54:06.313Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/r79ngfdb56","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/r79ngfdb56"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Oliver","last_name":"March","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Next Generation Sequencing"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"92s3365tfn","title":"EGFRvIII sequencing data","description":"To make the EGFRvIII mutant cell line in H9, gene editing was performed using CRISRP-CAS9 with two sgRNAs.\nThis is the sequencing data for EGFR site for mutant cell line.\nOff-target position of each sgRNA and  deep sequencing raw data\n\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-07-28T08:37:22.666Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/92s3365tfn","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/92s3365tfn"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"hyun mun","last_name":"kim","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Gene Sequencing"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"97zwpbfzdm","title":"NGS analysis of HTT editing in vitro and in vivo","description":"Tables S2-S3: Next-generation sequencing (NGS; MiSeq) analysis of on-target editing evaluating deletions and insertions (indels) in the CRISPR-HTT group in vitro and in vivo.\nFor each experiment (in vitro and in vivo), the dataset is composed of an excel file giving for each read, the length, the alignment score (to the reference sequence), the CIGAR string and whether indels were detected closed to expected cleavage site or not.\nTables S4-S5: Potential off-target sites for sgHTT and sgCas9 were assessed with the Bioconductor package CRISPRseek with default parameters. The tables report the potential off-targets for each sgRNA with a score equal or above 1. \n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2017-08-22T07:39:37.567Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/97zwpbfzdm","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/97zwpbfzdm"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Nicolas","last_name":"Merienne","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Gabriel","last_name":"Vachey","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nicole","last_name":"Déglon","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Molecular Neuroscience"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"tmkn3zsjts","title":"Secondary Library Validation Surface PrPC - Undifferentiated","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the custom secondary validation CRISPR/Cas9 KO library performed in undifferentiated  CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_Low or Brie_PrPC_High to indicate whether these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC Low\" or \"PrPC High\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the paired function to compare high and low samples directly.  ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:24.211Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/tmkn3zsjts","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/tmkn3zsjts"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vs9fwhbcvj","title":"Genome-wide Brie CAD5 Surface PrPC - Differentiated PrPC High","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 KO library (Brie) performed in differentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_High to indicate that these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC High\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the biological replicates function to compare between \"PrP Low\" and \"PrP High\" samples.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:42.171Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vs9fwhbcvj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vs9fwhbcvj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"p5t6d78zn8","title":"Genome-wide Brie CAD5 Surface PrPC - Differentiated PrPC Low","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 KO library (Brie) performed in differentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_Low  to indicate that these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC Low\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the biological replicates function to compare between \"PrP Low\" and \"PrP High\" samples.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:58.456Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/p5t6d78zn8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/p5t6d78zn8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"5pfdty7zd6","title":"Genome-wide Brie CAD5 Surface PrPC  - Undifferentiated","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 KO library (Brie) performed in undifferentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_Low or Brie_PrPC_High to indicate whether these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC Low\" or \"PrPC High\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the biological replicates function to compare \"PrP Low\" and \"PrP High\" samples directly.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:32.252Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/5pfdty7zd6","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/5pfdty7zd6"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"6r7spc5x6f","title":"CRISPR off-target sequencing analysis","description":"Exome sequencing on two independent models of myeloid neoplasms was performed to query off-target effects of Cas9 nuclease. Aligned sequencing data was filtered for reads overlapping predicted off-target cut sites (as determined by algorithm by Hsu et al., 2013) and 161 hematopoiesis and leukemia genes recurrently mutated in hematologic malignancies. Bam files of the filtered sequencing reads for each sample, as well as all of the annotations required for filtering is included.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2017-09-19T20:27:54.778Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/6r7spc5x6f","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/6r7spc5x6f"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Zuzana","last_name":"Tothova","orcid":null},{"first_name":"John","last_name":"Krill-Burger","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Benjamin","last_name":"Ebert","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["DNA Sequencing"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"jb89dp34d8","title":"Secondary Library Validation Surface PrPC - Differentiated","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the custom secondary validation CRISPR/Cas9 KO library performed in  differentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_Low or Brie_PrPC_High to indicate whether these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC Low\" or \"PrPC High\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the paired function to compare high and low samples directly.  ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:18.673Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/jb89dp34d8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/jb89dp34d8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":140249,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":185,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":140249,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":139478,"restricted":70,"embargoed":701},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2322},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":1336},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":701},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Centre","count":473},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":443},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":426},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y